  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 204.03 Commencement of Adjudicative Proceeding. If the matter between the division and the petitioner is not resolved within the 120-day period, the matter shall be considered a contested case within the meaning of RSA 21-J:28-b and the presiding officer shall issue a notice of hearing.\n\nSource. #4060, eff 5-29-86, EXPIRED: 5-29-92\n\nNew. #5423, eff 6-23-92; ss by #6749, eff 5-19-98, EXPIRED: 5-19-06\n\nNew. #8658-A, eff 6-13-06; ss by #11185-A, eff 9-20-16; ss by #12905, eff 10-23-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev200.html"
